DevOps Engineer (Operations Team)
We're always looking for the ones truly passionate about their work. If you are amongst them, you can rest assured there is a place for you in eMAG. We've grown very fast and are determined to keep doing so. What brought us here is our desire for continuous evolution and practical results.
More than 6000 colleagues are part of eMAG Teams. We strongly believe in people's development and therefore every year we invest more and more energy and resources to remain an organization that is constantly learning. We want to ensure that you'll have the most talented colleagues and the proper environment to grow and achieve great results, to become what you desire on a personal and professional level. Join us, grow faster!
 What you’ll have to do:
Transitioning applications to Kubernetes and driving their migration to the cloud;
Partnering with development teams on production scaling, dependency upgrades, security patches, and performance improvements - building self-service tooling so teams can handle routine operations themselves;
Designing, developing and maintaining reusable CI/CD pipelines for automated, secure and scalable delivery;
Instrumenting services and infrastructure with metrics, dashboards, and actionable alerting (Prometheus, Grafana), including managing metric collection and cost;
Configuring and troubleshooting load balancing, service networking, and connectivity across services (HAProxy, gateways, Kubernetes networking) to increase system stability and reliability;
Investigating and resolving production incidents during working hours - tracing issues across application, network, and infrastructure layers, and contributing to postmortems and permanent fixes;
Identifying repetitive issues or tasks and implementing permanent solutions;
Defining and managing cloud infrastructure using Infrastructure as Code (IaC);
Administering the Linux systems underlying our container and cloud environments;
Documenting infrastructure configurations, deployment procedures, and operational runbooks.
 What makes you a good fit:
Have 3+ years of experience in DevOps or similar roles;
Have solid Linux administration skills;
Have very good knowledge of cloud environments, containers and container orchestration solutions (Kubernetes);
Have hands-on experience with at least one major cloud provider (AWS or Tencent preferred - our stack runs on both; GCP/Azure experience transfers well);
Have experience with Terraform for infrastructure as code;
Have solid understanding of networking concepts, operating systems, automation, distributed computing, high availability and security best practices;
Have practical experience with monitoring and logging in production - Prometheus and Grafana or equivalents.
 What makes you stand out: 
Experience building CI/CD pipelines in GitLab CI or GitHub Actions;
Scripting skills (Bash, Python, Go or similar);
Experience with Helm and custom chart development;
Experience with GitOps tooling (ArgoCD, Flux);
Experience with service mesh and API gateways (Envoy, kgateway, or similar);
Experience with secrets management (Vault or similar);
Experience with Terragrunt;
Advanced observability: distributed tracing and log aggregation;
Relevant certifications: CKA, CKAD, or equivalent cloud certifications.
 What we’ve prepared for you:
Medical subscription: Medicover or Regina Maria. 
A flexible budget that you can invest in yourself as you wish: meal tickets, holiday tickets, cultural vouchers, private pension, foreign language classes, eMAG, Fashion Days, Therme & Genius, membership to different gyms or even professional development classes. 
Different discounts from our partners: banking, mobile, dental medicine or wellness. 
Access to the Bookster library and free credits on the Hilio psycho-emotional health platform. 
An accelerated learning environment, with access to over 100.000 curated online resources and platforms, learning academies and development programs. 
New headquarters, where sleek design, natural light, and versatile spaces create an energizing and comfortable environment for hybrid work. 
